WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:02.670
- [Narrator] So I'm going
to write down a number

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.610
and I'm going to think about how much

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:08.280
do each of these digits of the number,

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.690
what value do they represent?

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.310
And actually, let me
pick on this two here.

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:14.930
What does that two represent?

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.250
Does it just represent two,

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.960
or does it represent something
different than just two?

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.810
Pause the video and think about that.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.280
All right, now we'll
think about it together.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.860
And actually I'm going to
start with the seven here.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.910
The seven is in the one's place.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:32.200
So this seven represents seven ones,

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.800
which is of course still just seven.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.920
So nothing too surprising there.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.150
Then we could go to the ten's place.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.690
So this one doesn't just represent one,

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.030
it represents one 10.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.180
Or another way to think
about it, it represents 10.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:52.180
And then this two, it is
in the hundred's place.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:53.620
So it doesn't just represent two,

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.940
it represents two hundreds,
we could write it that way,

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.490
or it represents the value 200.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:02.780
So the number here is 217.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:06.950
The two represents two hundreds or 200.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.160
Now let me give you a
slightly different question.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:12.920
I'm going to write down three numbers.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.150
So we have this number
and I'm intentionally

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.080
not saying it out loud, that number,

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:24.080
I have this number and I have this number.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:26.760
And what I want you to
do is pause the video

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.180
and tell me in which
of these three numbers

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.543
does the seven represent 70?

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:36.840
Pause the video and think about that.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.610
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:42.293
So let's start with this top number,

00:01:42.293 --> 00:01:45.380
In this number, the seven
is in the one's place,

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.940
so that seven really just
represents seven ones,

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:51.120
which is still just seven.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.640
So this seven does not represent 70.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.380
Now in this next number, the
two is in the one's place

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.330
and we see that the seven
is in the ten's place.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:06.760
So this actually represents seven tens.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:11.760
Well, seven tens is the same thing as 70.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:16.580
So it's actually in this second situation

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.800
where the seven does represent 70.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.580
This number is 572, the
seven represents 70.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:26.980
And let's just check
this last number here.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.010
Well, here are the seven
is not in the one's place,

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.270
not in the ten's place,

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.500
it is in the hundred's place.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.990
So this represents seven hundreds or 700.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.713
And that makes sense,
this number here is 705.

